From 2d7a4e793e10cecf514de8d87e73163f3a4e3a39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 08:04:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 132/135] media: i2c: add a GalaxyCore GC02M1 driver

Add a driver for the GalaxyCore GC02M1 2 MP sensor with one fixed mode:
1600x1200 RAW10 over one D-PHY lane at 672 Mbps from a 19.2 MHz MCLK.

The initialisation table is the vendor sequence of the Xiaomi Redmi Note
12 Turbo macro module; it ends with the MIPI output off, which stream on
enables after setting the stock mirror and flip (P0:0x17 = 0x83).

Controls: exposure (0x03/0x04), frame length through vertical blanking
(0x41/0x42, up to 0x3fff), read-only horizontal blanking (line length
2192), pixel rate and link frequency, and a total gain in 1/1024 units
that is split into an analogue step (0xb6) and a digital pre-gain
(0xb1/0xb2, 1024 = 1x). The analogue steps are those of the Rockchip
GC02M1 driver (Copyright (C) 2020 Rockchip Electronics Co., Ltd.,
GPL-2.0), as posted in https://github.com/armbian/linux-rockchip/pull/609.

Power sequencing follows the vendor module: reset asserted, DOVDD and
AVDD, reset released, MCLK and 6 ms before the first register access.
Runtime PM autosuspends after 2 s and keeps the sensor off for at least
1.2 s: a Qualcomm CCI master that stays clocked across a sensor power
cycle hangs until it reinitialises on runtime resume. The chip ID
(0xf0/0xf1 = 0x02e0) is checked again at stream start, with one retry.

Signed-off-by: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/Kconfig  |  12 +
 drivers/media/i2c/Makefile |   1 +
 drivers/media/i2c/gc02m1.c | 859 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 872 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/media/i2c/gc02m1.c

